.TH FACTER_C 1 "January 2026" "puppetc 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
facter_c \- Native system fact collection tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B facter_c
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFACT\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B facter_c
is a native fact collection tool that gathers system information and
outputs it in various formats. It is compatible with Puppet's facter
and can be used standalone or integrated with puppetc-agent.
.PP
Facts include information about the operating system, hardware, network
configuration, and more.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Output facts in JSON format.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yaml
Output facts in YAML format.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List all available fact names without values.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I FACT
One or more fact names to display. If no facts are specified,
all facts are displayed.
.SH AVAILABLE FACTS
The following facts are collected:
.SS System Information
.TP
.B hostname
System hostname
.TP
.B fqdn
Fully qualified domain name
.TP
.B kernel
Kernel name (e.g., Linux)
.TP
.B kernelrelease
Kernel version
.TP
.B uptime_seconds
System uptime in seconds
.TP
.B uptime_hours
System uptime in hours
.TP
.B uptime_days
System uptime in days
.SS Operating System
.TP
.B operatingsystem
Operating system name (e.g., Ubuntu, Debian)
.TP
.B operatingsystemrelease
Operating system version
.TP
.B osfamily
Operating system family (e.g., Debian, RedHat)
.TP
.B os
Structured fact with OS details
.SS Hardware
.TP
.B architecture
CPU architecture (e.g., x86_64)
.TP
.B processorcount
Number of CPU cores
.TP
.B memorysize_mb
Total memory in megabytes
.TP
.B memoryfree_mb
Available memory in megabytes
.TP
.B is_virtual
Whether the system is a virtual machine
.SS Network
.TP
.B ipaddress
Primary IP address
.TP
.B macaddress
Primary MAC address
.TP
.B networking
Structured fact with network interface details
.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
By default, facts are output in a human-readable text format:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hostname => myserver
ipaddress => 192.168.1.100
.fi
.RE
.PP
With \fB\-j\fR, facts are output as JSON:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
  "hostname": "myserver",
  "ipaddress": "192.168.1.100"
}
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Show all facts:
.PP
.RS
facter_c
.RE
.PP
Show specific facts:
.PP
.RS
facter_c hostname ipaddress osfamily
.RE
.PP
Output as JSON:
.PP
.RS
facter_c \-j
.RE
.PP
List available fact names:
.PP
.RS
facter_c \-l
.RE
.PP
Get a single fact value for scripting:
.PP
.RS
facter_c hostname
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Error
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR puppetc-agent (1),
.BR puppetc-compile (1)
